35,2,1,talk,May,,"@Shizue, your committee minutes confirm my suspicion: the ferry and rail back offices never agreed on data terms. That’s the real bottleneck, not the tech.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, the data bottleneck is real, but my rosters show the late-turn pool is already stretched thin. We cannot promise coverage we don’t have.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"@May, the data shows waiting for connections is the real time sink, not ticketing. We must fix the handoffs, not the machines.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"@May, you’re right. The data gap is a hidden wall. I also found two accessibility projects quietly reverted. We must ask who else must say yes before we promise dates.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The ledger shows a lapsed grant balance, but operating subsidies are trimmed. Ticketing fees now exceed paving budgets. We are funding the past, not the future.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, if the late-evening pilot hit its cost target, your “stretched thin” excuse is just bad management, not a structural flaw.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, I appreciate the optimism, but the data shows a third of our crews are missing. We cannot manage away a structural deficit.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, I hear your worry about the crew. But the data shows the delay is in the connections, not the platforms. We must fix the handoffs first.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, I understand your worry. But the accessibility records show some work was quietly undone. We must verify who else must agree before we promise dates.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, the deficit is real, but the fees are the trap. We are paying contractors more than we spend on actual infrastructure.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,"@Midori, fixing handoffs is smart, but if the back offices won’t share data, you’re just polishing a broken bridge.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, I concede the data point. But a bridge needs builders. If the crews are gone, your perfect handoff is just a theoretical exercise.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@May, I understand your caution. But the timed runs prove the platforms aren’t the bottleneck. We must trust the data to guide our next steps.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@May, you’re right. The data gap is a hidden wall. I also found two accessibility projects quietly reverted. We must ask who else must say yes before we promise dates.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@May, the data gap is real, but the financial bleed is worse. We cannot fix handoffs if we are bankrupt by the ticketing fees.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, you’re right, the fees are bleeding us. But without data sharing, we’re just paying for silence. Let’s fix the terms first.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
